# ============================================================================
# Grid Master — API keys & backend environment variables
# (this is the ONLY place keys are configured; never commit a real .env)
#
# Copy the ones you use into your host's dashboard (Vercel: Settings →
# Environment Variables. Netlify: Site settings → Environment variables),
# then REDEPLOY — variables only reach a new deployment.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Booking e-mail relay — see docs/booking-email-setup.md
#
# Configure exactly ONE provider. With it, every booking is:
#   a) e-mailed to your company inbox (MAIL_TO), and
#   b) the customer gets a thank-you confirmation mail FROM YOUR COMPANY with
#      their official booking receipt attached as a branded PDF (section 3).
#
# Without any provider the booking form still works via the FormSubmit
# fallback (needs a one-time activation) — but no customer confirmation or
# PDF can be sent automatically in that mode.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Brevo (https://brevo.com) — RECOMMENDED for this site.
# Free 300 mails/day. Lets you verify your existing Gmail address as the
# sender with one click (no domain needed), so customer e-mails arrive from
# "Grid Master Solar Systems <contactgridmaster@gmail.com>".
# Setup: Brevo → SMTP & API → API Keys → Generate. Then:
#   BREVO_API_KEY=<your key>
#   MAIL_FROM=Grid Master Solar Systems <contactgridmaster@gmail.com>
# and verify that Gmail under Brevo → Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs → Senders.
# BREVO_API_KEY=

# Resend (https://resend.com) — free 100 mails/day. The default
# onboarding@resend.dev sender can only mail YOUR OWN inbox; to e-mail
# customers you must add and verify a domain you own in Resend first.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# SendGrid (https://sendgrid.com) — free 100 mails/day. Supports "single
# sender verification" of a Gmail address (Settings → Sender Authentication).
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=

# Web3Forms (https://web3forms.com) — mails bookings to your inbox with zero
# sender setup, but CANNOT e-mail the customer (no confirmations, no PDF).
# WEB3FORMS_KEY=

# Any webhook that accepts a JSON POST (Google Apps Script, Zapier, n8n).
# Receives the booking + rendered mail + base64 PDF when a customer
# confirmation is sent through it.
# MAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Shared by every provider above
# MAIL_TO=contactgridmaster@gmail.com
# MAIL_FROM=Grid Master Solar Systems <contactgridmaster@gmail.com>

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Customer thank-you confirmation (PDF receipt attached)
#
# Enabled by default whenever a provider that can mail customers (1) is set.
# The mail thanks the customer, states the team member visiting, the date and
# the time slot, and attaches their booking receipt as a PDF — the same file
# the website offers as a download.
# Set to "off" to disable it without touching anything else:
# CUSTOMER_CONFIRMATION_EMAIL=off

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Customer bookings → Google Sheet logger (optional, independent of e-mail)
# See docs/customer-bookings-sheet-setup.md for the full click-by-click setup.
# Every booking is appended as a row to a Google Sheet you own — download it
# any time as a real .xlsx file (File → Download → Microsoft Excel).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Apps Script "Web app" URL from Step 5 of the setup guide.
# MUST end in /exec — a /dev URL is the private test URL and never works.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# The same secret you set as the SHARED_SECRET script property in Step 3.
# It must match EXACTLY (no quotes, no trailing space) or every booking is
# silently rejected by the script.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_SECRET=

# After changing any value you MUST redeploy — environment variables only
# reach a NEW deployment. Then check everything at:
#
#   /api/booking-health?selftest=1
#
# That endpoint is read-only, writes nothing to the sheet, never reveals the
# secret (only an 8-character fingerprint), and tells you in plain English
# which step is misconfigured.
